**/results/**/{inference,inferencing}*/
**/results/**
**/desktop.ini
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/

# Experiment run artifacts, in full. Nothing under the top-level
# experiments/ is ever committed -- not the payloads, not the figures, and
# not the metadata.json sidecars, 104 of which were previously tracked in
# violation of this rule. Every run is reproducible from its specification
# and seed; the store, not the repository, is where results live.
#
# The leading slash anchors this to the repository root and is load-bearing:
# an unanchored `experiments/` also matches notebooks/experiments/, which
# would silently exclude every experiment notebook from version control.
/experiments/

# The default content store. `mbl run` without `--store` and without
# $MBL_STORE writes to ./store (cli/app.py's DEFAULT_STORE), so any command
# issued from the repository root creates one here -- a 1.9 MB stray was
# deleted by hand during the vertical slice.
#
# The leading slash is load-bearing for the same reason it is above, and here
# the collision is not hypothetical: an unanchored `store/` would also match
# `src/mbl/store/` and `tests/store/`, silently untracking Tier 4 and its
# suite. The same unanchored-pattern trap has already cost this project a
# cold-start run (`rsync --exclude 'store'` dropped both of those directories
# and the run reported "no tests ran" rather than failing).
/store/

# Agent-local state. Not shared configuration: the accumulated entries carry
# per-session identifiers and absolute machine paths.
.claude/*
# ...except the workflows themselves, which are process this project reviews
# like any other document rather than machine-local habit. Note `.claude/*`
# and not `.claude/`: git cannot re-include a path under an excluded
# DIRECTORY, so the negation below would be unreachable.
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/hooks/

# Build and tooling caches.
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/

# Executed notebooks are build artifacts (D9): git tracks the output-free
# source, the rendered copy is regenerated.
**/*.nbconvert.ipynb
**/*-executed.ipynb
